* ============================================================================
* Trafo_PA_Entrada - estimated linear model of QRP Labs T201, 2026-10-21.
* Created for Landell; NOT a manufacturer-supplied or measured transformer model.
* Source winding data: Documentos/PA_Assembly_200.pdf, section 3.5, pp. 11-12.
* Original core: BN61-2402; primary 6 turns, bifilar secondaries 3 + 3 turns.
*
* Inductance reference, used as an estimate for this core size/material:
* https://fair-rite.com/product/multi-aperture-cores-2861002402/
* Fair-Rite specifies AL >= 160 nH/turn^2, tested at 10 kHz, low flux.
* Taking this catalog minimum as a starting assumption gives LP=36*160nH
* = 5.76uH and each secondary half LS=9*160nH=LP/4=1.44uH.
* These are NOT measured PA values or guaranteed inductances at RF.
*
* Symbol Type X; subcircuit name Trafo_PA_Entrada.
* Terminal order matches Trafo_PA.qsym:
*   PRI1 PRI2 SEC1 SEC2 SEC3; SEC2 is the center tap, normally DRIVER_BIAS.
* Dotted ends: PRI1 and SEC1. With positive mutual coupling, the second
* half is oriented SEC2 -> SEC3. Thus SEC1 and SEC3 carry opposite RF
* polarities relative to SEC2. Ideal turns ratio is 6:3:3, or 1:1 end-to-end.
*
* Adjustable assumptions, NOT core/winding specifications:
*   KC=0.999: same strong coupling for all three winding pairs.
*   RP=0.1 ohm: primary winding series resistance.
*   RS=0.05 ohm: series resistance of EACH secondary half.
* Finite resistance permits a DC path without an ideal zero-resistance loop.
* No internal ground or primary-secondary DC connection is added.
*
* Not modeled: core loss, frequency-dependent permeability/resistance,
* winding capacitance, interwinding capacitance, saturation or temperature.
* Leakage is represented only through KC. Losses are only the stated RP/RS.
* This model is for initial functional tests; RF accuracy is unvalidated.
* QSPICE runtime testing is pending and remains user-run.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT Trafo_PA_Entrada PRI1 PRI2 SEC1 SEC2 SEC3 PARAMS: LP=5.76u KC=0.999 RP=0.1 RS=0.05
RPRI PRI1 P_DOT {RP}
LPRI P_DOT PRI2 {LP}
RSECA SEC1 SA_DOT {RS}
LSECA SA_DOT SEC2 {LP/4}
RSECB SEC2 SB_DOT {RS}
LSECB SB_DOT SEC3 {LP/4}
KPA LPRI LSECA {KC}
KPB LPRI LSECB {KC}
KAB LSECA LSECB {KC}
.ENDS Trafo_PA_Entrada

* ============================================================================
* Trafo_Driver_Saida - estimated linear model of QRP Labs T202, 2026-10-22.
* Created for Landell; NOT a manufacturer-supplied or measured transformer model.
* Source winding data: Documentos/PA_Assembly_200.pdf, section 3.6, pp. 13-14.
* Original core: BN61-2402; bifilar primary 3 + 3 turns, secondary 5 turns.
* Uses the same inductance-reference assumption as Trafo_PA_Entrada above:
* https://fair-rite.com/product/multi-aperture-cores-2861002402/
* AL=160 nH/turn^2 is a catalog minimum at 10 kHz, used as a starting estimate.
* LPH=9*160nH=1.44uH is the inductance of EACH primary half, not the total.
* LS=LPH*(5/3)^2=4uH. At perfect coupling the full primary is 4*LPH=5.76uH.
* These are NOT measured PA values or guaranteed inductances at RF.
*
* Symbol Type X; subcircuit name Trafo_Driver_Saida.
* Terminal order matches Trafo_Driver_Saida.qsym:
*   PRI1 PRI2 PRI3 SEC1 SEC2; PRI2 is the primary center tap.
* In the PA, PRI2 receives the driver drain supply; no supply is built in.
* Dotted ends: PRI1 and SEC1. The lower primary half is oriented PRI2 -> PRI3.
* Equal/opposite primary-end voltages relative to PRI2 add magnetically.
* Ideal full-primary to secondary turns ratio: (3+3):5 = 6:5.
* Balanced DC currents flowing from PRI2 to the primary ends oppose in the core.
*
* Adjustable assumptions, NOT core/winding specifications:
*   KC=0.999: same strong coupling for all three winding pairs.
*   RP=0.05 ohm: series resistance of EACH primary half, as in T201's 3 turns.
*   RS=0.0833333333 ohm: estimated 5-turn secondary resistance, scaled from
*                      the assumed 3-turn resistance by 5/3, same wire basis.
* Finite winding resistance provides a DC path without ideal zero-ohm loops.
* Use LPH>0, RP>0, RS>0 and 0<KC<=1; all three inductors share the same core.
* No internal ground or primary-secondary DC connection is added.
*
* Not modeled: core loss, frequency-dependent permeability/resistance,
* winding/interwinding capacitance, saturation, DC-imbalance effects or heating.
* Leakage is represented only through KC; losses are only the stated RP/RS.
* Intended for initial functional tests; RF accuracy is unvalidated.
* QSPICE runtime testing is pending and remains user-run.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT Trafo_Driver_Saida PRI1 PRI2 PRI3 SEC1 SEC2 PARAMS: LPH=1.44u KC=0.999 RP=0.05 RS=0.0833333333
RPRIA PRI1 PA_DOT {RP}
LPRIA PA_DOT PRI2 {LPH}
RPRIB PRI2 PB_DOT {RP}
LPRIB PB_DOT PRI3 {LPH}
RSEC SEC1 S_DOT {RS}
LSEC S_DOT SEC2 {LPH*25/9}
KPAB LPRIA LPRIB {KC}
KPAS LPRIA LSEC {KC}
KPBS LPRIB LSEC {KC}
.ENDS Trafo_Driver_Saida

* ============================================================================
* POT - generic linear potentiometer for Landell, 2026-10-23.
* Symbol Type X; subcircuit name POT; terminal order matches Pot.qsym:
*   A = upper end, B = lower end, W = wiper.
* Instance parameters: RT=4.7k POS=0.5 (defaults shown).
* RT is the total A-to-B track resistance in ohms; use RT > 0.
* POS is the fractional wiper position, nominally from 0 to 1:
*   POS=0 places W at B; POS=1 places W at A; POS=0.5 is the midpoint.
* R(A,W)=RT*(1-P); R(W,B)=RT*P; their sum remains RT.
* P is internally clamped to [1e-6, 1-1e-6] to avoid zero-ohm branches
* at either endpoint and to bound out-of-range POS values.
* Each endpoint therefore retains 1 ppm of RT (4.7 milliohms at 4.7k).
* Static linear track only: no contact noise/resistance, parasitics,
* tolerance, temperature dependence, power limits or mechanical behavior.
* No internal ground connection. QSPICE runtime testing remains user-run.
* ============================================================================

.SUBCKT POT A B W PARAMS: RT=4.7k POS=0.5
.PARAM PINT={min(max(POS,1e-6),1-1e-6)}
RAW A W {RT*(1-PINT)}
RWB W B {RT*PINT}
.ENDS POT
